The bot-facing half of the seasonal-intervals feature. Closes #67.

Settings screen (SeasonalMenuService):
  - sendScreen renders the global config: enabled toggle, mode picker
    (MULTIPLIER ● / FIXED ○), per-season values that you can cycle by
    tapping. Status line shows current season (computed by SeasonResolver)
    so the user sees what's in effect right now.
  - toggleEnabled / setMode / cycleMultiplier / cycleInterval /
    clearInterval — each persists and re-renders. EditMessageText with
    SendMessage fallback (same pattern as the weather screen).
  - MULTIPLIER_STEPS = 0.5..1.5 by 0.1, INTERVAL_STEPS = {1,2,3,5,7,10,
    14,21,28,35,45,60}. Tap cycles through. Compromise vs full numeric
    wizard — keeps a pet-project feature in pet-project complexity.
  - Plain text, no markdown (the parens-around-multiplier rendering
    would clash with V1 markdown otherwise; learned that from #69).

Menu integration:
  - Settings menu gains a «🍂 Сезонные интервалы» row between
    «🌦 Погода» and «⬅️ Назад».
  - MenuCallbackService gets MENU:SEASONAL case + SEASON: prefix
    routing. Inner switch on parts[1]: TOGGLE / MODE:{MULTIPLIER,FIXED}
    / MUL:{SUMMER,WINTER} / INT:{SUMMER,WINTER}[:CLEAR]. Plus a parse-
    error / unknown-action default with answerCallback feedback.
  - Wrapped in try-catch with diag-log at entry, mirroring the
    handleWeatherCallback pattern from #69. Same null-check on the
    service bean as belt-and-suspenders against DI breakage.

Dispatcher (PlantsCareBot):
  - SEASON_CALLBACK_PREFIX = «SEASON:» added to the whitelist. Without
    this the buttons would silently fall off the cliff — exact symptom
    we just debugged in the weather feature. Adding to whitelist is
    now the third step in the muscle-memory checklist.

Per-plant override (PlantCardService):
  - Edit-menu row «🍂 Сезонность: Наследовать/Включена/Выключена».
  - cycleSeasonalOverride: INHERIT → ON → OFF → INHERIT on each tap,
    saves Plant, re-renders the edit menu. The full state cycles in
    three taps, no nested screens.
  - PLANT:SEASONAL:<plantId>[:LOC:<locId>] callback parses plantId
    and optional back-target, delegates to the service.

Card display:
  - In the «📅 Напоминания» block of the plant summary, if seasonal
    is active for that plant and the effective interval differs from
    the base, the line gets a suffix:
        «• Полив каждые 10 дн. (сейчас лето → 8 дн.)»
    Same call shape as the integration-layer code (effectiveIntervalDays
    with plant + user). Pure read — no side effects.
  - formatSeasonalOverride helper centralizes the «Наследовать /
    Включена / Выключена» strings for the button label.

No new unit tests — every piece of business logic was tested in 1/3
(SeasonResolverTest + SeasonalIntervalServiceTest, 27 cases combined).
This commit is mostly UI plumbing — calling those services and
rendering text/keyboards. The dispatcher whitelist registration is
the bit most likely to bite in future, but the WARN-log for
unhandled prefixes (added in #69) covers that diagnostically.
